<title>POLAND: Polish KPW clears Amica Wronki for public trade.</title>
<headline>Polish KPW clears Amica Wronki for public trade.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) has cleared for public trade the 2,184,500-share initial public offering of household appliances maker Amica Wronki SA, the KPW said in a statement.</p>
<p>The firm's 6,553,000 existing shares have also been approved for trade.</p>
<p> Tranches		  No Of Shares	   Subscription</p>
<p>			     Offered		  Period</p>
<p> Large-investor	  1,795,000		May 30-June 3</p>
<p> Small-investor	    289,500		June 2-9</p>
<p> Closed			100,000		June 2-9</p>
<p> Lead Manager:	   BMT SA brokerage</p>
<p> Minimum price* (PLN): 28/shr  Lead Underwriter:     n/a</p>
<p> Use Of Proceeds:	paying back its long-term loans,</p>
<p>			     investments</p>
<p>Note: * - price as estimated by the firm, the final issue price will be set through book-building. The company seeks a main market listing.</p>
<p> EARNINGS DATA	   1996		     1995</p>
<p>(in million of PLN)</p>
<p> Net profit:	     25.3		     0.4</p>
<p> Sales:		   361.9		   191.9</p>
<p>Main Shareholders:</p>
<p>Bank Handlowy SA  - 44.4 pct of shares or 47 pct of votes on shareholders meeting</p>
<p>Polish Fabryka Armatury Sp z oo - 31.7 pct of shares or 33.5 percent of votes</p>
<p>No of existing shares: 13,106,000</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
